Z||000000||Master_Sushi||12-12-2000||04:09 PM||||Whenever I use my parking brake, my blue chime thing dings. Is it suppose to make a<BR>noise with the parking brake on?  If so... Is there any way to make it shut up when I use the Parking Brake?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Phil||12-12-2000||04:47 PM||||Take the keys out of the ignition.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/New-sig_1.jpg"> <BR>SC 3800||||reg||1
Z||000002||JetroGT||12-12-2000||05:15 PM||||Just remove the plastics and the lever boot. Then unplug the switch. If you do this and have a stick shift you will loose the ability to pop the trunk with the engine running. ||||reg||14
Z||000003||theogre||12-12-2000||08:26 PM||||Yes, it's suposed to do that.<P>It's not hard to kill a chime tone. read my cave article. It's very easy to leave the brake pulled slightly and drag a set of pads to death without that chime and light working. Depending on just how you sit and how you position the tilt steering wheel the light may not be very visible. It's not like other cars where you can visibly see the brake handle out of place.<P>A better solution so you can work in the car might be to put a switch in the brake signal wire to the chime. Then you can silence it while you work but turn it back on for safety later.||||reg||1
Z||000004||jerpro||12-14-2000||11:06 PM||||do 84 se's have the chime thing?<BR>IF they do Mine is either broken or I am deaf. (probably both)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
